os","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/katre/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2021-08-09T10:32:49Z","updated_at":"2021-10-12T20:02:18Z","closed_at":"2021-10-12T19:55:22Z","author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Description of the problem / feature request:\r\n\r\nWhen building using using the `--cpu=custom_cpu` flags, I get my artifacts in the `bazel-out/custom_cpu-<opt|dbg>` folder.\r\nHowever, when I use the new platforms flag, my build artifacts always end up in `bazel-out/k8-<opt|dbg>`, so the path is completely independent of the platform. This results in builds for different platforms clobbering each other's intermediate artefacts and effectively changing incremental builds into full builds. \r\n\r\nI would expect that when I'm using `--platform=custom_platform`, then the build artifacts should end up in `bazel-out/custom_platform-<opt|dbg>` and not default to k8 CPU name. Alternatively there should be some way to specify the output path for a custom platform.\r\n\r\n### Bugs: what's the simplest, easiest way to reproduce this bug? Please provide a minimal example if possible.\r\n\r\nRun any build using platform flag in a project with more than one platform\r\n\r\n### What operating system are you running Bazel on?\r\n\r\nCentos 8 Stream\r\n\r\n### What's the output of `bazel info release`?\r\n\r\nrelease 4.1.0\r\n\r\n###  Have you found anything relevant by searching the web?\r\n\r\n No.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"bazel-io","id":15028808,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1MDI4ODA4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15028808?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/user